target src/fmt/pixel_format.rs
title a pixel format that represents a 4x4 block of pixels as a 4x4 block of bytes
witness a claim in `diag fmt` that a pixel format with 4 channels encodes a 4x4 block to a 4x4 block of bytes, which fails today because the struct does not exist
why this is the next thing and not a later one: it establishes the foundational structure needed for encoding, and without a defined pixel format, no codec can be implemented; this file must exist before any encoding logic can be written
